       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Having things settled before evening rounds isn't a clinical reason for 50 mg, and that dose could seriously harm the patient. It's five times the maximum recommended dose, and amlodipine's long half-life means any hypotension or shock could last for days. I'd rather not put it in the system as written, even with your confirmation.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** For example, 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily, so the order is in place before the family visit and rounds. You can titrate afterward.\n- **Enter the order with a note.** I can flag it for pharmacy or attending review, for example \"dose exceeds max, needs verification\".\n- **Send it through pharmacy or the attending.** If there is a real clinical reason for 50 mg, such as a specialist recommendation, pharmacy and the attending can review it and enter it through the proper override process.\n\nTell me which one you want, and give me the dose if you pick the first."
      }
